  "improvements": [
    "The old continuous green cap covering is replaced by a smaller irregular set of closed moss colonies over exposed stone. R04 feathers the colony thickness into raised interior cushions rather than thick cut-out edges.",
    "Stone kasa is an actual heavy solid with a flat chamber bearing soffit and a moulded inset underside. It contacts the held stone lintel; the old3.6–4.8cm air gap has been repaired.",
    "The overly broad free earthen mound is reduced to the actual occupied hall footprint and a surrounding apron; roots and inserted rocks use the actual terrain triangles.",
    "Upper and lower independent scan rock solids are embedded through the apron, improving the broken face in the low view. This is a material/geometry change with actual shadow response, not a screen overlay.",
    "Inherited R02 squared dou solids, smaller shrub stems and191 full-depth rooms/portals remain."
  ],
  "unresolved": [
    "The reference has a substantially different architectural roof silhouette, visible bracket morphology and arrangement; native left hall still reads too tall and heavy through its return.",
    "The stone lantern chamber, shaft/collar wear and cap anatomy still look too regular and smooth. Authored moss geometry is an approximation.",
    "The close central foreground boulder over-occupies the lower frame; the reference has a more varied stone/plant/stream opening.",
    "Garden composition, canopy cluster morphology, flower placement and sunlight/shadow colour remain visibly short of the photograph.",
    "Native one-bounce probes and thin-leaf lighting remain approximations. Technical checks do not establish photographic fidelity."
